ingredient_count: 3
---

Prepare work area to protect surfaces.

Plan size and design of geometry if desired. Prime #art board{} if untreated.

Mix 1 part @PVA glue{1%part} and 1 part @white acrylic paint{1%part} until smooth.

Add 2 parts @Plaster of Paris{2%parts} and mix until smooth. Add up to another 1 part of @Plaster of Paris{1%part} testing as mixing for desired consistency.

Once consistency is achieved the art fun can start. If using a #profile texture tool{} spread some paste in shape where the pull will take place.

Pull the texture paste along the shape/path of design. Scrape off if a redo is desired.

Add other texture techniques, experimenting with various #palette knife{} and tools.

Once the design is complete let dry slowly.

Colour or metallic finish can then be added where desired. Let dry.

Place in #frame{} or hang unframed. Enjoy!

> Wood or MDF panel board in desired size can be used as the art board.